LineComment   "// The bitwise contract on the integers: band/bor/bxor combine two bit patterns"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// and shl/shr shift, the same width-blind way the arithmetic works — a result"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// that does not fit its type overflows at the assignment, exactly as + and *"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// do, so a shift never wraps. They are methods on every integer kind, not"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// operators. There is no native complement: ~x within a width is x.bxor(T.Max),"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// built in pure belt on these. All fold at compile time."
Newline       "\n"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// and / or / xor on a byte. The result of any of the three fits the width."
Newline       "\n"
